<p>Ah, dammit, I've accidentally reloaded the page.<br />
Here goes take 2.</p>
<p>Hi! I'm Kleo.<br />
I go by he/him or they/them pronouns, both are equally fine.</p>
<p><strong>Why/how did I join the site</strong><br />
I've been lurking on-and-off here for years. Not sure how long exactly, but long enough that I can't remember how I first found the SCP community. It's occupied a part of my mind for a long time. I've had some ideas for anomalies, and also wanted to vote on some criminally good posts, so I've decided to make an account.</p>
<p><strong>What do I want to do on the site?</strong><br />
Probably lurking for the most part. Commenting occasionally. Possibly writing. I'm not sure what combination of those things I'll do, so I'm using this thread instead of writing or reading. I've also got a list of skips that I've been intending to upvote.</p>
<p><strong>What are some hobbies I have?</strong><br />
I enjoy reading and watching films, particularly horror, thrillers, and sci-fi (no surprise there). I like drawing too, and my total inability to draw proportions correctly just makes me better at drawing spooky stuff. I also really like this one website: <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/">http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/</a> its like a creepy fictional organization that imprisons/contains supernatural entities. You probably haven't heard of it.</p>
<p><strong>Any concerns or worries about the site I have?</strong><br />
I don't know, it seems like the site is set up well and the mods are helpful. No concerns I can think of immediately.</p>
<p><strong>What kind of random thoughts keep you up at night?</strong><br />
Typically, just imagining hypothetical scenarios and deciding how they'd play out. Not sure why I do this, but I have been doing it for as long as I can remember. Also, as of late, something resembling depression. This is what zero physical interaction does to a mf.<br />
(Seriously though quarantine has been absolutely horrible for my mental health, as I'm sure it has been for everyone else. I'm not used to being constantly unhappy, or even anything less than optimistic. Ever since [REDACTED]virus made it so I can't talk to people in person, I realized how much I rely on those interactions for my happiness.)</p>
<p>That's about it. Probably a slog to read because I'm not a great writer. Hopefully it wasn't too bad.</p>

