<p>I&#8230;think my biggest concern about this idea is that it feels too much like it's pulling back the curtain around pattern screamers to reveal that they're just generic murder monsters: this feels like it'd be stronger if everything was almost exactly as it is now except there's no entity.</p>
<p>My other concern is that the plot feels very much like a generic sort of, horror/slasher film plot; where there's a monster gradually picking off the characters until only a few are left; and&#8230;I think it's not a huge deal here just because the actual progression is so bizarre and surreal; but I do think this means you're heavily relying on actually nailing doing indescribable horror well which can be really hard to do.</p>
<p>I'm&#8230;going to <span style="color: green">greenlight</span> this though just because I do genuinely think this can work and that you have a good idea of how you're going to pull it off.</p>

