						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13900591/abiogenesis-scp">Abiogenesis (SCP)</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842204">
									

<blockquote>
<p>The SCP is a (now neutralized) spatial anomaly in the outer-reaches of the solar system in the form of an Einstein–Rosen bridge (aka wormhole)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>IMO: this would be easier to write if the SCP was the ancient spacecraft; and then we worked backwards from the notes on the spacecraft to figure out what happened.</p>
<p>Or well, actually, if I was to give advice on writing this, my suggestion would be: really, strongly consider whether this would be best as a tale from the perspective of the crew.</p>
<p>I'm&#8230;really kinda hesitant on this exclusively because the idea feels&#8230;somewhat common? It's a relatively cliche time loop story where we seed our own planet that's somewhat reminiscent of stuff like Interstellar but on a bit of a larger scale; and it feels like this really needs some kind of unique spin on this beyond just the foundation's involvement to make it more interesting to a reader.</p>
<p>It might just need a little bit more narrative heft to it: perhaps there's question of like, where the Einstein-Rosen bridge came from that could have weight if answered, though it may be hard to not end up making something which feels very Mass Effect Reaper like if you do that.</p>

							</div>

								
					
